---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { url } from '../lib/utils';
---

<PageLayout title="About — Clean Snacks" description="Why Clean Snacks exists — real food, five ingredients or fewer, made in your kitchen.">
  <article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 py-12 sm:py-16">
    <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold text-dark-text mb-6">Why Clean Snacks exists</h1>

    <div class="prose prose-bark dark:prose-invert max-w-none">
      <p>
        Flip over any packaged snack and read the ingredients. Even the ones marketed as healthy — protein bars, veggie chips, organic fruit snacks — carry ingredient lists longer than most recipes on this site.
      </p>

      <p>
        Clean Snacks started with a simple question: <strong>what if you just made it yourself?</strong>
      </p>

      <p>
        Not a meal-prep marathon. Not a weekend project. Just real ingredients, basic tools, and a few minutes of your time. The kind of food that existed before the snack industry did.
      </p>

      <h2>What we stand for</h2>

      <h3>Every Ingredient Earns Its Place</h3>
      <p>
        If you can't identify it on sight or find it at a regular grocery store, it doesn't belong in your snack. No protein isolates. No maltodextrin. No "natural flavors."
      </p>

      <h3>Five Ingredients or Fewer</h3>
      <p>
        The shorter the ingredient list, the more likely you are to actually make it. Most of our recipes use three to five whole foods. Some use two. Simplicity is the point.
      </p>

      <h3>No Refined Sugar</h3>
      <p>
        We sweeten with Medjool dates, raw honey, pure maple syrup, and ripe bananas — whole sources that carry minerals and fiber alongside the sweetness.
      </p>

      <h3>Fuel, Not Filler</h3>
      <p>
        Every recipe is built around ingredients that give you something back — nuts, seeds, cacao, coconut, sea salt. Real food, not empty calories.
      </p>

      <h3>For Every Age and Every Moment</h3>
      <p>
        Packing a lunchbox. Fueling a workout. Reaching for something during a movie. We organize by occasion because that's how snacking actually works.
      </p>

      <h2>What we're not</h2>
      <p>
        Not a diet. Not a supplement brand. Not a calorie counter. When you eat real food in its whole form, your body handles the rest. The goal is simple: know exactly what you're eating because you made it yourself.
      </p>

      <p>
        <a href={url('/recipes/')}>Browse the recipes</a> and see how little you actually need.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</PageLayout>
